review.parity:
Bit-exact:
- template_search (the cell f_hz/ppm/tau0/drift/segment, chunks, cells; lam to 2e-16 relative; Z to 1.8e-15) on every probe: TINY and SHORT, weak/gate/noise, 250 Hz with its mix, out of reach, PassbandStore, CW-voted accumulators (OOK and FSK majorities), a 0.25 Hz/min plus 7.5 ppm candidate;
- the false-alarm recheck: 40 TINY and 42 SHORT noise captures with identical cells, |dZ| at most 5.5e-14, no detection on either side;
- _search_chan, _candidates, _search_input, _from_passband, and the refusal types and texts, including the noise floor's ZeroDivisionError/ValueError on 0- and 1-sample 250 Hz captures.

Within tolerance:
- receive_template on TINY: f_hz 1.8e-12 Hz, z 0, report fields within 1e-11;
- receive_template on SHORT with CW-known keying: ppm 2.7e-5 relative, z 4.1e-6, f_hz 2.2e-8 Hz. This is track's finite-difference refine_timing amplifying last-ulp differences, not em_search, so it is held to 1e-4 in the slow test;
- retro_detect log numbers within 0.11.

Not compared:
- a complex128 250 Hz capture (the C++ refuses it with NotImplementedError);
- aarch64 and MSVC builds (the AVX2 clone and scalar path agree here, other ISAs were not run).

review.notes:
I reviewed the retro lane at d764b8b (diff from 89653b9) line by line against sstvae/qrss/em.py lines 518-763: core, binding, rows and tests.

Two real bugs found and fixed in 202433d:
- **Eager 250 Hz noise floor.** The floor was taken before the reach test, so a too-short capture with every candidate out of reach raised where Python returns nothing.
- **Seam rule turned to "".** The associate seam's None rule came back as "", because the binding converted it to a C++ string.

The parity file gained:
- CW-voted and drifting-candidate cases: fast on TINY, slow on SHORT;
- the short-capture refusal and out-of-reach checks;
- an all-seams retro case.

Every new assertion was mutation-checked.

Checked and found no bug:
- the strict > and NaN handling;
- the reach test;
- the L band-centre offset in the stored list;
- the KeyError on a seam's missing segment;
- log formatting;
- Python-store routing in the rows;
- GIL handling: nogil core, seams take the GIL, Held deleters take the GIL;
- cancel: polled before each slot and each (segment, candidate); associate is atomic per find, so a cancel never leaves a half-written record;
- MSVC: the clones are GCC/Clang x86 only, and the fallback is std::fma plus the scalar np::abs; check_includes is clean.

I did not edit the skeleton or EM lane files. The bt/emr1 and bt/emr2 directories in the scratchpad belong to another lane's run and were left alone. Nothing was pushed.

